//! The outbound port for {{resource_pascal}} storage — declared by the domain.
//!
//! This is the half of hexagonal architecture that inverts the dependency. The domain
//! says what it needs in its own vocabulary, and a driven adapter in
//! `adapter/outbound/` supplies it. Postgres, an in-memory map and a test double are
//! then interchangeable, and none of them appears inside the hexagon.
//!
//! Note what this is *not*: a generic `Repository<T, Id>`. It talks about
//! {{resource_plural}}, returns {{resource_plural}}, and fails with domain errors. A
//! generic one would drag storage concepts back across the boundary it exists to defend.

